nexorable fate\", explanation: \"无情的命运\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"inevitable\", essence: \"不可避免的\" }, { word: \"relentless\", essence: \"无情的（主动）\" }, { word: \"inexorable\", essence: \"不可阻挡的（被动，无法劝阻）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"in + exor（说服）+ able = 不可说服的\", \"联想：orator 演说家，exor = 说动\"], visualHint: \"巨大的滚石从山上滚下，无法阻止\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"inexorable 强调'无法劝阻'，不是简单的'无情'\", \"常见搭配：inexorable decline/rise\"],\n    summary: \"inexorable = 不可阻挡的，无法阻止的\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"blight\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/blaɪt/\", us: \"/blaɪt/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"blight\", meaning: \"枯萎病，破坏因素\", origin: \"中古英语，可能与古北欧语相关\" }], explanation: \"blight = 植物枯萎病 → 破坏因素，祸害\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"健康的事物受到侵害\", feature: \"像植物感染枯萎病一样衰败\", result: \"被破坏或毁损\", essence: \"破坏性的祸害\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"祸害\", example: \"the blight of unemployment\", explanation: \"失业的祸害\" }, { context: \"破坏\", example: \"blight the landscape\", explanation: \"破坏景观\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"plague\", essence: \"瘟疫（大规模）\" }, { word: \"curse\", essence: \"诅咒（超自然）\" }, { word: \"blight\", essence: \"枯萎祸害（渐进性破坏）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"blight 听起来像'不赖'→ 其实很赖/恶劣\", \"联想：植物枯萎病，叶片上出现黑斑\"], visualHint: \"枯萎的植物上布满黑斑\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"blight 可作名词（祸害）和动词（破坏）\", \"urban blight = 城市衰败\"],\n    summary: \"blight = 祸害，破坏因素；使枯萎\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"unmask\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ʌnˈmɑːsk/\", us: \"/ʌnˈmæsk/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"un-\", meaning: \"去除\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"mask\", meaning: \"面具\", origin: \"法语 masque\" }], explanation: \"unmask = 去掉面具 → 揭露，暴露真面目\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"某人戴着面具隐藏真面目\", feature: \"摘下面具露出真实面貌\", result: \"真相被揭露\", essence: \"揭露隐藏的真相或本质\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"揭露\", example: \"unmask a fraud\", explanation: \"揭露骗局\" }, { context: \"暴露\", example: \"unmask the conspiracy\", explanation: \"揭露阴谋\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"expose\", essence: \"暴露（中性）\" }, { word: \"reveal\", essence: \"揭示（自然显露）\" }, { word: \"unmask\", essence: \"揭露伪装（强调去除面具）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"un + mask = 摘下面具\", \"联想：面具被扯下的瞬间\"], visualHint: \"面具被一把扯下，露出真面目\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"unmask 有戏剧性色彩\", \"与 reveal 相比，unmask 强调'欺骗被揭穿'\"],\n    summary: \"unmask = 揭露，暴露真面目\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"armor\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˈɑːmə(r)/\", us: \"/ˈɑːrmər/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"armor\", meaning: \"盔甲，装甲\", origin: \"拉丁语 armatura\" }], explanation: \"armor = 盔甲 → 保护，装甲\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"面临攻击或伤害的风险\", feature: \"穿上防护装备\", result: \"获得物理或象征性保护\", essence: \"保护性的盔甲或屏障\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"盔甲\", example: \"a suit of armor\", explanation: \"一套盔甲\" }, { context: \"装甲\", example: \"armor-plated vehicle\", explanation: \"装甲车\" }, { context: \"防护\", example: \"emotional armor\", explanation: \"情感上的防护\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"shield\", essence: \"盾牌（可移动的防护）\" }, { word: \"protection\", essence: \"保护（抽象）\" }, { word: \"armor\", essence: \"盔甲/装甲（全面覆盖的防护）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"arm + or = 武装/护甲\", \"联想：army 军队，arm 武装\"], visualHint: \"中世纪骑士穿着全身盔甲\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"英式拼写为 armour\", \"armor 可引申为心理上的'铠甲'\"],\n    summary: \"armor = 盔甲，装甲，保护\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"unravel\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ʌnˈrævl/\", us: \"/ʌnˈrævl/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"un-\", meaning: \"解开\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"ravel\", meaning: \"缠绕\", origin: \"荷兰语 ravelen\" }], explanation: \"unravel = 解开缠绕 → 拆解，揭开\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"复杂的事物缠绕在一起\", feature: \"逐根抽丝解开\", result: \"谜团或问题被理清\", essence: \"从纠缠中理出头绪\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"揭开谜团\", example: \"unravel the mystery\", explanation: \"揭开谜团\" }, { context: \"拆解\", example: \"unravel a sweater\", explanation: \"拆开毛衣\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"solve\", essence: \"解决（得到答案）\" }, { word: \"untangle\", essence: \"理清（物理上的）\" }, { word: \"unravel\", essence: \"拆解揭开（从缠绕中逐步理清）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"un + ravel（缠绕）= 解开缠绕\", \"联想：ravel = 缠绕，unravel = 拆开\"], visualHint: \"毛线团被一点点抽出来\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"unravel 既可指物理拆解也可指抽象揭穿\", \"unravel 也可指'崩溃瓦解'（被动）\"],\n    summary: \"unravel = 拆解，揭开，理清\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"mend\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/mend/\", us: \"/mend/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"mend\", meaning: \"修补，改善\", origin: \"古英语 menden\" }], explanation: \"mend = 修补破损 → 修理，改善\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"物品或关系出现破损\", feature: \"通过修补使其恢复\", result: \"回到可用或良好状态\", essence: \"修补破损，使之恢复\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"修理\", example: \"mend a broken chair\", explanation: \"修好破椅子\" }, { context: \"愈合\", example: \"the bone is mending\", explanation: \"骨头正在愈合\" }, { context: \"改善\", example: \"mend their relationship\", explanation: \"改善他们的关系\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"repair\", essence: \"修复（偏机械）\" }, { word: \"heal\", essence: \"治愈（偏身体）\" }, { word: \"mend\", essence: \"修补（简单修复，也指关系改善）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"mend 听起来像'慢的'→ 慢慢修补\", \"常见搭配：mend fences（修补关系）\"], visualHint: \"缝补衣服上的破洞\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"mend 比 repair 更口语化\", \"on the mend = 正在恢复中\"],\n    summary: \"mend = 修补，修理，改善\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"iconic\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/aɪˈkɒnɪk/\", us: \"/aɪˈkɑːnɪk/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"icon\", meaning: \"偶像，图标\", origin: \"希腊语 eikōn（画像）\" }, { part: \"-ic\", meaning: \"形容词后缀\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"iconic = 如偶像般的 → 标志性的，象征性的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"某事物具有极高辨识度\", feature: \"代表了一种文化或时代的符号\", result: \"成为经典象征\", essence: \"标志性的，具有符号意义\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"标志性的\", example: \"an iconic building\", explanation: \"标志性建筑\" }, { context: \"经典的\", example: \"an iconic movie scene\", explanation: \"经典电影场景\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"classic\", essence: \"经典的（经久不衰）\" }, { word: \"famous\", essence: \"著名的\" }, { word: \"iconic\", essence: \"标志性的（具有符号象征意义）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"icon（图标/偶像）+ ic = 如偶像般的\", \"联想：手机上的 app 图标 = icon\"], visualHint: \"埃菲尔铁塔——巴黎的标志性符号\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"iconic 强调'符号性'而非仅仅'有名'\", \"不是所有著名的都是 iconic\"],\n    summary: \"iconic = 标志性的，象征性的\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"predominant\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/prɪˈdɒmɪnənt/\", us: \"/prɪˈdɑːmɪnənt/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"pre-\", meaning: \"在前\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"domin\", meaning: \"统治\", origin: \"拉丁语 dominari\" }, { part: \"-ant\", meaning: \"形容词后缀\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"predominant = 在前面统治的 → 占主导地位的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"多个因素或力量并存\", feature: \"其中一个明显占优势\", result: \"成为最突出或最重要的\", essence: \"占主导地位的，最显著的\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"主要的\", example: \"the predominant color\", explanation: \"主要颜色\" }, { context: \"占优势的\", example: \"predominant opinion\", explanation: \"主流观点\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"dominant\", essence: \"支配的（强调控制力）\" }, { word: \"primary\", essence: \"首要的（强调排序）\" }, { word: \"predominant\", essence: \"占主导的（强调数量或程度优势）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"pre + dominant = 提前支配 → 占主导\", \"联想：dominate 统治\"], visualHint: \"饼图中占最大的一块\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"predominant 偏重'数量或程度上的优势'\", \"与 dominant 不同，predominant 不一定有控制意味\"],\n    summary: \"predominant = 占主导地位的，主要的\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"tongue\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/tʌŋ/\", us: \"/tʌŋ/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"tongue\", meaning: \"舌头，语言\", origin: \"古英语 tunge\" }], explanation: \"tongue = 舌头 → 语言，口才\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"舌头是发音的器官\", feature: \"通过舌头说出语言\", result: \"tongue 引申为语言或口才\", essence: \"舌头；引申为语言或口才\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"舌头\", example: \"burn one's tongue\", explanation: \"烫到舌头\" }, { context: \"语言\", example: \"mother tongue\", explanation: \"母语\" }, { context: \"口才\", example: \"a sharp tongue\", explanation: \"利嘴，说话刻薄\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"language\", essence: \"语言（抽象系统）\" }, { word: \"speech\", essence: \"言语（表达行为）\" }, { word: \"tongue\", essence: \"语言/舌头（文学或习语用法）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"mother tongue = 母语\", \"slip of the tongue = 口误\"], visualHint: \"伸出的舌头\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"tongue 作'语言'用时较文学化\", \"注意习语：hold one's tongue（保持沉默）\"],\n    summary: \"tongue = 舌头，语言，口才\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"scorch\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/skɔːtʃ/\", us: \"/skɔːrtʃ/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"scorch\", meaning: \"烧焦，烤焦\", origin: \"中古英语，可能与古法语 escorchier 相关\" }], explanation: \"scorch = 高温烧灼 → 烤焦，使枯萎\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"高温或烈日照射\", feature: \"表面被烧灼变色\", result: \"出现焦痕或枯萎\", essence: \"高温灼烧导致焦损\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"烤焦\", example: \"scorch the shirt with an iron\", explanation: \"熨斗烫焦了衬衫\" }, { context: \"晒枯\", example: \"the sun scorched the grass\", explanation: \"太阳把草晒枯了\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"burn\", essence: \"燃烧（完全过程）\" }, { word: \"char\", essence: \"烧黑（碳化）\" }, { word: \"scorch\", essence: \"烤焦（表面灼伤）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"scorch 听起来像'烧吃'→ 烧了吃 → 烤焦\", \"联想：scorched earth policy（焦土政策）\"], visualHint: \"烈日下枯黄的草地\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"scorch 强调表面灼伤，不是完全烧毁\", \"scorching hot = 酷热\"],\n    summary: \"scorch = 烤焦，烧灼，晒枯\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"abandon\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/əˈbændən/\", us: \"/əˈbændən/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"a-\", meaning: \"向\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"bandon\", meaning: \"控制，权力\", origin: \"古法语 bandon（控制权）\" }], explanation: \"abandon = 放弃控制 → 抛弃，遗弃\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"某人或某物受你控制\", feature: \"主动放弃对它的控制权\", result: \"被丢弃或遗弃\", essence: \"主动放弃，抛弃\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"抛弃\", example: \"abandon a pet\", explanation: \"遗弃宠物\" }, { context: \"放弃\", example: \"abandon the project\", explanation: \"放弃项目\" }, { context: \"放纵\", example: \"dance with abandon\", explanation: \"尽情跳舞\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"desert\", essence: \"遗弃（强调背弃义务）\" }, { word: \"forsake\", essence: \"抛弃（文学用语）\" }, { word: \"abandon\", essence: \"抛弃/放弃（最常用，也可指放纵）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"a + ban（禁止）+ don = 禁止掌控 → 放弃\", \"with abandon = 尽情地，放纵地\"], visualHint: \"荒野中被遗弃的房屋\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"with abandon = 放纵地（正面含义）\", \"abandon 与 abandon（放纵）是同词多义\"],\n    summary: \"abandon = 抛弃，放弃，放纵\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"eminent\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˈemɪnənt/\", us: \"/ˈemɪnənt/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"e-\", meaning: \"出\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"min\", meaning: \"突出\", origin: \"拉丁语 minere\" }, { part: \"-ent\", meaning: \"形容词后缀\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"eminent = 突出的 → 杰出的，著名的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"某人在某个领域表现出色\", feature: \"突出于众人之上\", result: \"享有盛誉和地位\", essence: \"在领域中杰出的\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"杰出的\", example: \"an eminent scientist\", explanation: \"杰出的科学家\" }, { context: \"显赫的\", example: \"eminent position\", explanation: \"显赫的地位\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"prominent\", essence: \"突出的（可以是位置）\" }, { word: \"famous\", essence: \"著名的（不一定因为成就）\" }, { word: \"eminent\", essence: \"杰出的（因成就而受人尊敬）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"e + min（突出）+ ent = 突出的\", \"注意区分：imminent（迫在眉睫的）\"], visualHint: \"一位受人尊敬的教授站在讲台上\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"eminent ≠ imminent（迫在眉睫的）\", \"eminent 强调因专业成就而受尊敬\"],\n    summary: \"eminent = 杰出的，显赫的\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"confound\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/kənˈfaʊnd/\", us: \"/kənˈfaʊnd/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"con-\", meaning: \"完全\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"found\", meaning: \"倾倒\", origin: \"拉丁语 fundere\" }], explanation: \"confound = 完全倾倒混合 → 使混淆，使困惑\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"两种事物本应分开\", feature: \"被混在一起无法分辨\", result: \"产生困惑或错误\", essence: \"使混淆困惑\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"使困惑\", example: \"confound the researchers\", explanation: \"让研究人员困惑\" }, { context: \"使混淆\", example: \"confound two concepts\", explanation: \"混淆两个概念\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"confuse\", essence: \"使困惑（常用）\" }, { word: \"bewilder\", essence: \"使迷惑（程度更深）\" }, { word: \"confound\", essence: \"使混淆（强调搞混，偏正式）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"con + found = 全倒在一起 → 搞混\", \"confound it! = 该死！（口语感叹）\"], visualHint: \"两杯水倒在一起，分不清哪杯是哪杯\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"confound 比 confuse 更正式\", \"confound 可作诅咒语：confound it!\"],\n    summary: \"confound = 使混淆，使困惑\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"cohort\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˈkəʊhɔːt/\", us: \"/ˈkoʊhɔːrt/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"co-\", meaning: \"共同\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"hort\", meaning: \"围场\", origin: \"拉丁语 hortus（花园/围场）\" }], explanation: \"cohort = 同一围场中的人 → 同伴，群体\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"一群人共同经历某事\", feature: \"属于同一批次或群体\", result: \"彼此具有同伴关系\", essence: \"同伴群体，同批人\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"同伴\", example: \"his cohorts in crime\", explanation: \"他的犯罪同伙\" }, { context: \"群体\", example: \"a cohort of students\", explanation: \"一届学生\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"companion\", essence: \"同伴（个人）\" }, { word: \"group\", essence: \"群体（中性）\" }, { word: \"cohort\", essence: \"同批群体/同伴（可带贬义）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"co + hort = 共同围场 = 同一批人\", \"联想：cohort study = 队列研究\"], visualHint: \"同一期入伍的士兵站在一起\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"cohort 可带贬义（同伙）\", \"学术用语中指'队列/同批研究对象'\"],\n    summary: \"cohort = 同伴，同伙，群体\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"intimate\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˈɪntɪmət/\", us: \"/ˈɪntɪmət/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"intim\", meaning: \"最内部的\", origin: \"拉丁语 intimus（最内部的）\" }, { part: \"-ate\", meaning: \"形容词后缀\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"intimate = 最内部的 → 亲密的，私密的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"关系深入到内心层面\", feature: \"彼此了解最内在的部分\", result: \"形成极亲密的关系\", essence: \"亲密的，深入内心的\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"亲密的\", example: \"intimate friends\", explanation: \"密友\" }, { context: \"私密的\", example: \"intimate details\", explanation: \"私密细节\" }, { context: \"暗示\", example: \"intimate that...\", explanation: \"暗示...\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"close\", essence: \"亲近的\" }, { word: \"personal\", essence: \"个人的\" }, { word: \"intimate\", essence: \"亲密的（涉及内心深处的）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"intim（最内部）+ ate = 最内心的 → 亲密的\", \"动词读音不同：/ˈɪntɪmeɪt/（暗示）\"], visualHint: \"两个人在烛光下低声交谈\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"形容词和动词读音不同\", \"intimate 作动词意为'暗示'，不是'使亲密'\"],\n    summary: \"intimate = 亲密的，私密的；暗示\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"interspecific\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˌɪntəspɪˈsɪfɪk/\", us: \"/ˌɪntərspɪˈsɪfɪk/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"inter-\", meaning: \"在...之间\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"specific\", meaning: \"物种的\", origin: \"拉丁语 species\" }], explanation: \"interspecific = 物种之间的 → 种间的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"不同物种生活在同一环境\", feature: \"物种之间产生互动\", result: \"形成种间关系（竞争/共生等）\", essence: \"不同物种之间的\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"种间的\", example: \"interspecific competition\", explanation: \"种间竞争\" }, { context: \"物种间\", example: \"interspecific hybrid\", explanation: \"种间杂交\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"intraspecific\", essence: \"种内的（同种内）\" }, { word: \"ecological\", essence: \"生态的\" }, { word: \"interspecific\", essence: \"种间的（不同物种之间）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"inter + specific = 之间 + 物种 = 种间的\", \"与 intraspecific（种内的）对比记忆\"], visualHint: \"两种不同的鸟在争夺同一棵树上的食物\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"interspecific vs intraspecific 是生物学重要对比\", \"specific 在此意为'物种的'（species相关）\"],\n    summary: \"interspecific = 种间的，物种之间的\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"rudimentary\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˌruːdɪˈmentri/\", us: \"/ˌruːdɪˈmentri/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"rudi\", meaning: \"粗糙，原始\", origin: \"拉丁语 rudis（粗糙的）\" }, { part: \"-ment\", meaning: \"名词后缀\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"-ary\", meaning: \"形容词后缀\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"rudimentary = 粗糙的初始状态 → 基本的，初步的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"某事物刚起步\", feature: \"只有最基本最粗糙的形式\", result: \"还不够完善或高级\", essence: \"最基本的，初步的\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"基本的\", example: \"rudimentary knowledge\", explanation: \"基本知识\" }, { context: \"初步的\", example: \"rudimentary equipment\", explanation: \"初步的设备\" }, { context: \"退化的\", example: \"rudimentary organs\", explanation: \"退化器官\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"basic\", essence: \"基础的（中性）\" }, { word: \"elementary\", essence: \"初等的\" }, { word: \"rudimentary\", essence: \"初步的（暗示不够完善）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"rude（粗糙）+ mentary = 粗糙的 → 初步的\", \"联想：rude 的词根就是'粗糙'\"], visualHint: \"一个简陋的草棚 vs 精美的房屋\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"rudimentary 可带贬义（简陋的）\", \"在生物学中指'退化的'（如退化器官）\"],\n    summary: \"rudimentary = 基本的，初步的，简陋的\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"downturn\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/ˈdaʊntɜːn/\", us: \"/ˈdaʊntɜːrn/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"down\", meaning: \"向下\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"turn\", meaning: \"转向\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"downturn = 向下转 → 衰退，下降\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"经济或状况原本向好\", feature: \"趋势突然向下转变\", result: \"进入低迷期\", essence: \"由好转差的下降趋势\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"经济衰退\", example: \"an economic downturn\", explanation: \"经济衰退\" }, { context: \"下降\", example: \"a downturn in sales\", explanation: \"销售额下降\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"recession\", essence: \"衰退（正式经济术语）\" }, { word: \"decline\", essence: \"下降（通用）\" }, { word: \"downturn\", essence: \"下行拐点（强调趋势转变）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"down + turn = 向下转\", \"与 upturn（上升）对应\"], visualHint: \"折线图从高处向下弯曲\" },\n    pitfalls: [\"downturn 强调趋势的'转折'\", \"常用搭配：economic downturn\"],\n    summary: \"downturn = 衰退，下降趋势\"\n  },\n  {\n    word: \"contributory\",\n    phonetic: { uk: \"/kənˈtrɪbjətəri/\", us: \"/kənˈtrɪbjətɔːri/\" },\n    root: { components: [{ part: \"con-\", meaning: \"共同\", origin: \"\" }, { part: \"tribut\", meaning: \"给予，贡品\", origin: \"拉丁语 tribuere\" }, { part: \"-ory\", meaning: \"形容词后缀\", origin: \"\" }], explanation: \"contributory = 共同给予的 → 促成的，起作用的\" },\n    logic: { premise: \"一个结果由多个因素导致\", feature: \"其中某个因素起到了促进作用\", result: \"该因素是结果的部分原因\", essence: \"促成的，起作用的\" },\n    usage: [{ context: \"促成因素\", example: \"contributory factors\", explanation: \"促成因素\" }, { context: \"起作用的\", example: \"contributory negligence\", explanation: \"混合过错（法律术语）\" }],\n    distinction: [{ word: \"contributing\", essence: \"贡献的\" }, { word: \"causal\", essence: \"因果的\" }, { word: \"contributory\", essence: \"促成的（部分原因，偏法律/正式）\" }],\n    memory: { methods: [\"contribute + ory = 贡献的 → 促成的\", \"联想：contributory factor = 促成因素\"], visualHint: \"多根箭头指向同一个结果，每根都是 contributory\" },\n    pitfalls: